<section class="py-5">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="mb-2">Claude plays Minesweeper</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Play it yourself (click to reveal, right-click or Flag mode to flag) or let Claude try. Claude sees the board as text and picks up to five moves per turn. The page enforces the rules, so it can't cheat and has to reason its way out.</p>
    <div class="ms-grid">
      <div>
        <div id="ms-board" class="ms-board" aria-label="Minesweeper board"></div>
        <div id="ms-status" class="mt-2 font-weight-bold"></div>
        <button id="ms-toggle" class="btn btn-primary mt-2">Let Claude play</button>
        <button id="ms-new" class="btn btn-outline-secondary mt-2 ml-2">New game</button>
        <button id="ms-flagmode" class="btn btn-outline-secondary mt-2 ml-2" aria-pressed="false">Flag mode</button>
        <div id="ms-cost" class="small text-muted mt-2"></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h5>What it's thinking</h5>
        <ul id="ms-log" class="list-unstyled small" style="max-height:420px; overflow:auto;"></ul>
        <h5 class="mt-4">Claude's notebook</h5>
        <p class="small text-muted mb-1">After each loss Claude writes itself a lesson. Lessons are saved only in this browser and shown to Claude in later games.</p>
        <ul id="ms-notes" class="small pl-3"></ul>
        <button id="ms-clearnotes" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary">Clear notebook</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

